Subject: Hide the running medium, name drives by /dev node, report open errors

ISO Image Writer lists every removable or USB block device UDisks2
reports, in the hash order of its GetManagedObjects reply, names each by
its UDisks2 object path, and writes on when OpenDevice fails.

- Skip a block device whose org.freedesktop.UDisks2.Block HintIgnore is
  true (udev's UDISKS_IGNORE), the mark a system puts on the medium it
  runs from; Dolphin and the Device Notifier already hide it.
- List the devices in object-path order, so the list and the drive
  selected first are the same on every launch.
- Show each drive by its /dev node (Block.Device), not its object path:
  "/dev/sdb - QEMU HARDDISK (8.0 GiB)".
- Check the OpenDevice reply and the QFile open, and report the error
  text ("Could not open /dev/sda: ...") instead of failing on the first
  block with "-1 of 1,048,576 bytes".
- Name the chosen drive, by the same display name, in the confirmation
  before writing.

